WEBVTT

00:15.420 --> 00:17.250
Is it morning already?

00:22.310 --> 00:24.860
What? "Just like an alarm clock"?

00:24.860 --> 00:27.610
I wonder what an alarm clock is.

00:29.590 --> 00:32.910
Morning, Sora. You seem 
energetic again this morning.

00:36.500 --> 00:39.590
Well, then, today we continue our journey!

00:58.160 --> 01:06.420
<b>The Weakest Tamer
Began a Journey
to Pick Up Trash</b>

02:10.990 --> 02:15.990
<b>Toward an
Unexpected Situation</b>

02:17.910 --> 02:19.780
Thank you for this food.

02:25.960 --> 02:27.560
It's so good!

02:27.800 --> 02:28.910
Sora, is yours good, too?

02:30.180 --> 02:31.620
You stretched taller!

02:32.590 --> 02:33.750
You jumped!

02:33.750 --> 02:36.050
Sora, you have new ways you can move!

02:37.700 --> 02:42.630
Somehow... you seem more sturdy 
than you used to.

02:43.280 --> 02:47.610
Sora, didn't you used to 
be weaker and more fragile?

02:49.030 --> 02:53.440
Maybe you've grown. You've eaten 
a lot of blue potions, after all.

02:56.080 --> 02:58.110
If you're healthier, 
I guess it doesn't matter why.

02:58.110 --> 02:59.850
Eat lots more, all right?

03:03.140 --> 03:05.450
I'm so glad I was able to 
gather so many fruits.

03:05.450 --> 03:08.930
I'm just about to run out of dried meat.

03:09.480 --> 03:13.230
When we reach the next village, Latom, 
I'll have to buy more dried meat.

03:13.230 --> 03:17.300
I need to catch some field mice 
to earn the money to do that.

03:18.020 --> 03:23.370
What? "If I cook and eat the meat I catch, 
it will cost less money"?

03:23.370 --> 03:25.390
I can't do that.

03:25.390 --> 03:28.460
If I take the time to cook 
meat out in the forest,

03:28.460 --> 03:30.520
the smell will draw in monsters.

03:30.990 --> 03:34.790
Even if it costs money, 
buying dried meat is safer.

03:37.330 --> 03:39.730
What? You've already eaten all of them?

03:40.480 --> 03:43.450
Those were all the potions I had.

03:45.120 --> 03:46.820
You still want more?

03:48.040 --> 03:49.910
What do I do?

03:54.980 --> 03:56.120
Oh!

03:56.770 --> 03:58.070
A dumping ground!

04:00.140 --> 04:02.470
There might be food for Sora here!

04:03.170 --> 04:04.600
Oh! Clothes!

04:04.600 --> 04:07.140
I've been wanting a change of clothes.

04:08.120 --> 04:11.150
Oh, right. Your food comes first, doesn't it?

04:13.140 --> 04:13.770
I found some!

04:14.660 --> 04:16.230
Potion bottles!

04:18.320 --> 04:20.370
We're lucky there are so many of them!

04:21.910 --> 04:24.050
This one still seems new.

04:24.850 --> 04:27.160
And this one is too old.

04:27.160 --> 04:29.050
Sora, you won't eat this, will you?

04:30.500 --> 04:32.390
What? You'll eat that?

04:32.390 --> 04:35.270
Maybe as long as it's a blue potion,
 nothing else matters?

04:35.800 --> 04:37.460
This is an inexpensive bottle.

04:37.460 --> 04:40.160
A child must have made 
this potion as practice.

04:40.160 --> 04:41.170
How about this one?

04:43.490 --> 04:45.220
You'll eat that one, too.

04:47.060 --> 04:49.040
Oh! That's a red one!

04:49.040 --> 04:51.240
It's a red potion that cures illnesses!

04:52.600 --> 04:55.340
You eat red potions, too?

04:55.340 --> 04:57.440
You wouldn't eat them before, though.

04:57.860 --> 04:59.390
Well, what about this, then?

04:59.390 --> 05:01.680
It's a green potion that dulls pain.

05:02.870 --> 05:04.710
So, you won't eat green ones.

05:04.710 --> 05:05.950
Then how about this one?

05:05.950 --> 05:08.300
It's a purple potion that breaks curses.

05:09.040 --> 05:11.390
You won't eat purple ones, either?

05:11.390 --> 05:14.220
What? "Mix the colors"?

05:14.590 --> 05:16.550
All right. I'll try it!

05:17.130 --> 05:19.520
Mix blue and red, and then...

05:19.520 --> 05:20.560
How about this?

05:21.750 --> 05:22.980
You ate it!

05:22.980 --> 05:25.070
Then what about the purple one from before?

05:27.350 --> 05:29.510
A similar color won't cut it, huh?

05:37.970 --> 05:40.650
It's lucky that we have 
such nice weather, isn't it?

05:41.880 --> 05:44.230
I feel like we'll be able to 
travel really far today!

05:45.370 --> 05:48.570
I never imagined that traveling 
would be this much fun.

05:49.460 --> 05:51.830
I'm so glad that I met you, Sora.

05:51.830 --> 05:57.360
I thought that I'd always travel alone, 
that I'd always live all alone.

05:57.360 --> 05:59.850
What? "You're not alone"?

05:59.850 --> 06:02.670
But my past life is still me in the end.

06:03.460 --> 06:05.600
Oh! Those are noberries!

06:05.600 --> 06:07.260
And there's so many of them!

06:08.750 --> 06:11.500
They're delicious!

06:11.500 --> 06:12.850
Sora, do you want some, too?

06:12.850 --> 06:13.800
Here!

06:15.560 --> 06:17.800
But they taste so good!

06:17.800 --> 06:19.780
I'm going to pick lots and lots!

06:28.910 --> 06:31.370
Thank you for this food!

06:33.860 --> 06:35.160
These taste so good!

06:35.160 --> 06:38.230
It'd be nice if we could travel down paths 
lined with noberries the whole way!

06:38.230 --> 06:40.170
Oh, but wild grapepes would be good, too!

06:41.400 --> 06:42.820
You already finished eating those?

06:42.820 --> 06:44.290
Do you want some more?

06:45.380 --> 06:46.790
Then, here you go.

06:50.800 --> 06:52.890
What?! You want to eat more?

06:52.890 --> 06:54.310
You're eating too much!

06:54.310 --> 06:57.850
If you keep eating like this, there won't 
be any left for me when I need them!

06:59.640 --> 07:02.150
All right! All right, I understand!

07:03.150 --> 07:07.000
Honestly! At this rate, 
Sora's going to eat them all.

07:07.000 --> 07:08.510
What do I do?

07:08.930 --> 07:12.180
What? "As long as you're awake, 
you'll get hungry"?

07:12.180 --> 07:15.410
I see. Then, I should have Sora 
fall asleep as soon as possible.

07:18.000 --> 07:19.710
Hey, Sora!

07:20.130 --> 07:21.950
I'm going to tell you a bedtime story.

07:26.930 --> 07:32.110
This is a story I heard a lot 
when I was little.

07:32.110 --> 07:34.050
I'll tell it to you now, Sora.

07:35.440 --> 07:39.890
Long, long ago, the world was at war.

07:40.410 --> 07:44.660
One day, the king gathered together 
magicians who could see the future

07:44.660 --> 07:47.530
and had them all make predictions 
about how the war would end.

07:51.060 --> 07:54.430
The future they saw was 
the end of the world.

07:55.310 --> 07:58.600
It was a such a terrifying sight.

07:59.620 --> 08:03.890
The magicians discussed their visions, 
and then, in order to protect the world,

08:03.890 --> 08:07.380
they cast a very, very powerful magic.

08:07.800 --> 08:11.320
No one now knows what that magic was,

08:11.320 --> 08:14.010
and no one now can use it.

08:14.010 --> 08:18.030
The only one who can is a child 
who comes from another world.

08:18.030 --> 08:19.890
It's a forgotten magic.

08:20.610 --> 08:23.900
It's a magic that doesn't 
exist anywhere anymore...

08:23.900 --> 08:26.180
A magic that no one remembers anymore...

08:26.180 --> 08:29.400
A magic that no one knows the effect of...

08:29.400 --> 08:32.050
A magic that doesn't exist...

08:32.420 --> 08:37.140
It's vast and scary and quiet...

08:37.140 --> 08:40.360
lonely and untouchable...

08:40.970 --> 08:42.440
a nothingness.

08:50.210 --> 08:52.470
Huh? Is it morning?

08:56.340 --> 09:00.260
What? I fell asleep while 
telling the bedtime story?

09:00.920 --> 09:04.340
Well, that story makes me sleepy.

09:04.340 --> 09:07.470
I've never heard it all the way to the end.

09:08.250 --> 09:09.110
Sora!

09:11.460 --> 09:13.350
They're gone! Gone!

09:13.350 --> 09:16.070
There isn't a single blue 
or red potion left!

09:17.910 --> 09:19.870
Honestly, Sora!

09:34.990 --> 09:36.390
All right! I caught it!

09:36.620 --> 09:39.210
It's such a big help that 
I can trade field mice for money.

09:39.210 --> 09:42.810
In order to continue our journey, I have 
to earn and save as much money as I can.

09:43.730 --> 09:45.350
A snake monster?

09:47.070 --> 09:49.730
It isn't a field mouse. What do I do?

09:50.730 --> 09:54.030
But I might be able to sell this too, so...

09:56.360 --> 09:58.370
Um... let's see.

10:01.620 --> 10:02.620
Take this!

10:12.250 --> 10:14.180
That should do it.

10:23.360 --> 10:25.350
I wonder what this smell is.

10:26.810 --> 10:31.100
Is it a monster? 
But I don't sense anything.

10:46.910 --> 10:48.260
Sora, hide!

10:48.260 --> 10:50.100
If there are bandits around, 
you'll be a target!

11:39.930 --> 11:42.760
That's... Latom over there.

11:48.150 --> 11:51.020
Wait just a moment, you two, there!

11:54.530 --> 11:56.380
I have to tell someone.

12:00.170 --> 12:02.080
Town Hall?

12:09.420 --> 12:11.610
I'm telling you, that's what 
that fighting stance is for!

12:11.610 --> 12:13.690
What? Is that true?

12:13.690 --> 12:15.950
Um, excuse me.

12:22.180 --> 12:24.810
Say, young man, what's that?

12:24.810 --> 12:25.720
What?

12:25.720 --> 12:27.160
Oh, nothing!

12:27.160 --> 12:31.660
I set a trap for field mice and
 caught this snake monster instead.

12:31.660 --> 12:34.940
If you want to sell a snake, you should 
go to an apothecary, not the town hall.

12:34.940 --> 12:37.810
Th-Thank you. No, wait!

12:37.810 --> 12:42.950
On my way here, I found some 
people who had passed away.

12:47.040 --> 12:50.250
Come closer. 
Will you tell me all the details?

12:50.250 --> 12:52.820
It was on the road from Latoto Village.

12:52.820 --> 12:53.980
There was a cart on fire,

12:53.980 --> 12:56.580
and there were people who had been 
attacked by monsters and didn't survive.

12:56.580 --> 12:58.170
What? Did you say monsters?

12:58.680 --> 13:01.930
If that's true, then there's a possibility 
that this village will be attacked.

13:10.340 --> 13:12.850
It's not that I'm doubting you,

13:12.850 --> 13:15.940
but was it really monsters and not bandits?

13:16.320 --> 13:19.880
Yes. The wounds to the bodies were awful,

13:19.880 --> 13:22.880
and the cart horses were dead, too.

13:23.370 --> 13:27.490
If it had been bandits, I think they'd have 
stolen the horses instead of killing them.

13:30.080 --> 13:33.090
This account is real. Monsters, huh?

13:34.410 --> 13:36.290
Apologies, but I have an urgent request!

13:36.290 --> 13:39.660
Find the exact location and, 
if possible, the type of monster!

13:39.660 --> 13:42.500
I'll put a formal request in 
through the Guild later!

13:42.500 --> 13:43.510
Sir!

13:45.140 --> 13:47.800
All right. Let's go!

13:47.800 --> 13:49.430
Hurry! Quit dawdling!

13:50.960 --> 13:52.940
Thank you, kid.

13:53.440 --> 13:57.060
You'll get the tip reward after we 
confirm the location. Is that all right?

13:57.430 --> 13:59.280
Tip reward?

13:59.280 --> 14:01.120
You can get money for information.

14:01.120 --> 14:04.390
If you have information about monsters or
people who have died from monster attacks

14:04.390 --> 14:07.140
and you bring those tips to a town hall, 
you'll receive a tip reward.

14:07.140 --> 14:08.740
I didn't know that.

14:08.740 --> 14:11.610
It's better to have information 
on monsters as quickly as possible.

14:11.610 --> 14:15.000
That way, we can take measures 
before people get hurt. Here.

14:22.290 --> 14:24.690
Please hold on to this document 
and come back again later.

14:24.690 --> 14:27.470
We should have the results 
of the investigation by this evening.

14:27.470 --> 14:31.090
All right. Thank you.

14:32.440 --> 14:37.230
The market value for a snake monster 
is two gidal per snake, however...

14:37.620 --> 14:41.610
this appears to be a female. 
They're rare, so I'll give you three gidal.

14:41.610 --> 14:42.570
What?

14:42.570 --> 14:44.360
<i>A gidal is...</i>

14:44.360 --> 14:47.850
<i>Ten copper blocks, which are 
100 dal each, make one gidal,</i>

14:47.850 --> 14:51.810
<i>so three gidal would be... 
30 field mice worth?!</i>

14:51.810 --> 14:54.120
<i>A snake monster is worth that much?!</i>

14:54.120 --> 14:56.820
What is it? Are you unhappy 
with three gidal?

14:56.820 --> 14:58.290
Oh, no! That will be fine.

15:00.010 --> 15:02.550
If you catch any more, 
bring them here for me.

15:06.230 --> 15:08.640
This is amazing! Three whole gidal!

15:08.640 --> 15:11.290
I'll be able to buy lots of dried meat 
for our journey with this!

15:12.470 --> 15:15.220
Next, let's go look for food for you, Sora!

15:20.260 --> 15:22.610
I wonder if there will be any potions here.

15:23.490 --> 15:25.740
Oh! That's a magic bag!

15:29.290 --> 15:30.940
There's one over there, too!

15:32.190 --> 15:33.330
And over here, too!

15:33.330 --> 15:35.830
There are <i>so many</i> magic bags!

15:38.830 --> 15:41.550
All together, there are 21 of them.

15:44.170 --> 15:47.050
I'd like to take anything 
that seems usable with me,

15:47.050 --> 15:49.560
but there's only so much 
I can carry while walking.

15:49.560 --> 15:52.980
And they're all older models, 
so their abilities are all different, too.

15:53.530 --> 15:56.630
What? "If you put the magic bags 
into other magic bags,

15:56.630 --> 15:58.500
you can carry as many as you want"?

15:58.500 --> 16:00.520
That's it! All right, then.

16:01.860 --> 16:04.950
It went in! And it's gotten lighter, too.

16:06.020 --> 16:08.990
Now, I'll put this into another magic bag!

16:11.200 --> 16:13.380
Huh? It won't go in.

16:13.380 --> 16:18.420
Maybe a magic bag that has a magic bag 
in it can't go into another magic bag.

16:20.130 --> 16:23.590
Oh, even an empty magic bag 
won't go into this one.

16:28.260 --> 16:32.750
It went into this one, 
but it didn't get any lighter.

16:32.750 --> 16:36.860
If I put lots into this one, it might get 
so heavy that I can't walk carrying it.

16:39.560 --> 16:42.970
Over here are magic bags 
that don't carry other magic bags.

16:42.970 --> 16:46.850
Here are the magic bags 
that can carry one magic bag.

16:46.850 --> 16:50.990
These are magic bags that can 
carry up to two magic bags.

16:50.990 --> 16:55.160
And these are magic bags that can 
carry up to three magic bags.

16:55.160 --> 16:56.240
Those groups each have...

16:56.240 --> 17:00.350
magic bags that can carry a magic bag 
with a magic bag in it,

17:00.350 --> 17:03.610
magic bags that make 
the things they carry lighter,

17:03.610 --> 17:07.550
and magic bags that don't make 
the things they carry lighter.

17:08.070 --> 17:12.530
So, if I put magic bags 
that can't carry magic bags

17:12.530 --> 17:15.560
into a magic bag that 
doesn't make things lighter,

17:15.560 --> 17:19.050
and then put that into a magic bag 
that does make things lighter,

17:19.050 --> 17:21.820
then the whole thing 
will be light and compact.

17:22.210 --> 17:26.690
But that would take a bag that can carry 
three bags and some can only hold one,

17:26.690 --> 17:30.780
so I'll put together the ones that can 
only hold one bag, and then...

17:31.470 --> 17:36.350
No, wait. If I leave the ones 
that carry two bags for last, then...

17:37.740 --> 17:42.560
After I put this one in this one, 
I put this one in next, and...

17:44.260 --> 17:47.230
No! There's still that one left!

17:47.230 --> 17:49.200
I have to do it over!

17:51.980 --> 17:54.180
I put this one in this one.

17:54.180 --> 17:57.180
And finally, I put this one in this one...

17:57.600 --> 17:59.600
I did it!

18:03.090 --> 18:05.400
Sorry to keep you waiting! 
Let's go collect potions!

18:21.870 --> 18:23.330
Hey there, kid!

18:25.720 --> 18:28.210
The information you gave 
us earlier really saved us.

18:28.210 --> 18:30.120
We were able to verify it right away.

18:30.120 --> 18:31.800
Really?

18:32.150 --> 18:34.850
The monsters were ogres and an ogre king.

18:34.850 --> 18:37.650
There were ogre tracks around the wagon,

18:37.650 --> 18:41.940
and when the adventurers followed them, 
they spotted the ogre king.

18:42.730 --> 18:46.130
Some of the higher-ranked adventurers 
are about to go hunt them down.

18:46.130 --> 18:49.400
It's dangerous, so don't leave the village 
until the monsters are defeated.

18:49.840 --> 18:51.110
I won't.

18:51.110 --> 18:54.080
And, since we verified your information, 
you'll get your tip reward.

18:54.590 --> 18:56.570
Please go to the town hall to accept it.

18:59.280 --> 19:01.830
That's a huge feather 
in your cap, young man!

19:01.830 --> 19:03.210
A feather in my cap?

19:03.210 --> 19:04.830
Do you have the document from earlier?

19:04.830 --> 19:05.840
Yes.

19:06.530 --> 19:07.660
It's...

19:09.230 --> 19:11.240
Um, I'm sure it's...

19:11.630 --> 19:15.450
It's in the one inside this one. No...

19:15.450 --> 19:18.340
It's inside the one I put in this one.

19:22.930 --> 19:24.870
Um... Here it is!

19:25.210 --> 19:25.980
Here!

19:27.980 --> 19:29.150
Yes. Indeed it is.

19:29.150 --> 19:30.230
Now then...

19:30.740 --> 19:33.820
the tip reward for information 
on five deceased persons is five gidal.

19:33.820 --> 19:35.530
That's one silver tablet.

19:35.530 --> 19:36.400
<i>Five gidal?!</i>

19:37.160 --> 19:41.570
<i>The snake monster was worth three gidal, 
which was 30 field mice worth.</i>

19:41.570 --> 19:44.880
<i>This time it's five gidal, 
so that's 50 field mice worth!</i>

19:44.880 --> 19:46.140
<i>It's worth that much?!</i>

19:47.090 --> 19:50.500
And for information on high-ranked monsters, 
your reward is two ladal.

19:50.500 --> 19:52.110
That's two gold coins.

19:52.110 --> 19:53.550
<i>Gold coins?!</i>

19:53.550 --> 19:55.630
<i>One ladal is worth ten gidal.</i>

19:55.630 --> 19:58.010
<i>And ten gidal is worth 1,000 dal,</i>

19:58.010 --> 19:59.510
<i>so two ladal would be...</i>

19:59.510 --> 20:01.860
<i>200 field mice worth?!</i>

20:01.860 --> 20:04.430
<i>All together, that's 250 field mice worth.</i>

20:04.430 --> 20:08.730
<i>And if I add what I got for the snake, 
it's 280 field mice worth!</i>

20:09.060 --> 20:11.650
It's a large sum, so be careful 
not to drop it anywhere.

20:12.730 --> 20:14.350
I, um...

20:14.350 --> 20:15.190
I will.

20:20.620 --> 20:22.700
W-Well, then...

20:25.960 --> 20:26.940
Wait.

20:31.970 --> 20:32.920
There's those.

20:39.080 --> 20:41.860
<i>This is the first time 
I've ever had so much money.</i>

20:46.030 --> 20:49.030
<i>Could it be that everyone is 
after these gold coins?</i>

20:49.450 --> 20:52.980
Why is that boy carrying so many bags?

21:17.420 --> 21:19.380
Here. This one's a red one.

21:22.850 --> 21:25.450
The forest is dangerous 
because of the monster hunt,

21:25.450 --> 21:27.510
so tonight we'll sleep here.

21:32.370 --> 21:35.990
I guess we'll have to stay in Latom 
until the monster hunt is over.

21:36.810 --> 21:39.330
The next place we're going 
is Latome Village.

21:39.330 --> 21:41.360
It seems like it'll be a big town.

21:41.360 --> 21:43.240
I wonder what kind of place it is.

21:45.600 --> 21:46.990
This might be sort of fun...

21:50.040 --> 21:51.660
this adventure-filled journey.

21:55.390 --> 21:57.920
When I'm with you, Sora, I have so much fun!
